The table structure information is (table names): 
['aliens_details', 'skills_dim', 'legislators_terms', 'cities_currencies', 'legislators', 'skills_job_dim', 'job_postings_fact', 'alien_data', 'cities_countries', 'legislation_date_dim', 'cities', 'aliens_location', 'aliens', 'cities_languages', 'job_company']
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their role  
• legislators.id_bioguide – personal key that lets us join the biographical table to the terms table.  
• legislators.gender – filter to only the female legislators (‘F’).  
• legislators_terms.id_bioguide – join‐key coming from the terms table.  
• legislators_terms.state – the 2‑letter state abbreviation that the member represented in that term.  
• legislators_terms.term_start – starting date of the term (YYYY‑MM‑DD). Used to decide which is the member’s very first term.  
• legislators_terms.term_end – ending date of the term (YYYY‑MM‑DD). Used to decide whether at least one of the member’s terms includes December 31st (the term must span across a year‑end or finish on/after 12‑31).  

Typical filter / logic conditions  
1. legislators.gender = 'F'    → keeps only the women.  
2. A term includes 31‑Dec if  
     CAST(substr(term_end,1,4) AS INT) > CAST(substr(term_start,1,4) AS INT)    – the term crosses a year boundary, therefore the member served on 31‑Dec of the start year, or  
     (CAST(substr(term_end,1,4) AS INT) = CAST(substr(term_start,1,4) AS INT)  
      AND substr(term_end,6,5) >= '12-31')                                       – single‑year terms that finish on/after 31‑Dec.  
3. The “first state” for a legislator is the state appearing in the ­minimum term_start belonging to her.  

Below are ten exploratory SQL statements, moving from simple inspection to the final answer.  
(Each query is different and limited to 20 rows so it can be run safely.)  

```sql
-- 1. What values appear in the gender column?
SELECT DISTINCT "gender"
FROM "legislators"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Show the first 20 women in the data set.
SELECT "id_bioguide",
       "full_name",
       "gender"
FROM "legislators"
WHERE "gender" = 'F'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Display every term served by the sample female legislator C000127 (Maria Cantwell).
SELECT *
FROM "legislators_terms"
WHERE "id_bioguide" = 'C000127'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Find terms that unquestionably include December 31st
--    (the term crosses a calendar year or ends on/after 12‑31).
SELECT "id_bioguide",
       "state",
       "term_start",
       "term_end"
FROM "legislators_terms"
WHERE (
          CAST(substr("term_end",1,4) AS INTEGER) >
          CAST(substr("term_start",1,4) AS INTEGER)
      OR (CAST(substr("term_end",1,4) AS INTEGER) =
          CAST(substr("term_start",1,4) AS INTEGER)
          AND substr("term_end",6,5) >= '12-31')
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Same as #4 but restricted to female legislators.
SELECT lt."id_bioguide",
       lt."state",
       lt."term_start",
       lt."term_end"
FROM "legislators_terms" AS lt
JOIN "legislators" AS l
  ON l."id_bioguide" = lt."id_bioguide"
WHERE l."gender" = 'F'
  AND (
        CAST(substr(lt."term_end",1,4) AS INTEGER) >
        CAST(substr(lt."term_start",1,4) AS INTEGER)
      OR (CAST(substr(lt."term_end",1,4) AS INTEGER) =
          CAST(substr(lt."term_start",1,4) AS INTEGER)
          AND substr(lt."term_end",6,5) >= '12-31')
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. List the distinct female legislators that satisfy the 31‑Dec condition.
SELECT DISTINCT lt."id_bioguide"
FROM "legislators_terms" AS lt
JOIN "legislators"      AS l
  ON l."id_bioguide" = lt."id_bioguide"
WHERE l."gender" = 'F'
  AND (
        CAST(substr(lt."term_end",1,4) AS INTEGER) >
        CAST(substr(lt."term_start",1,4) AS INTEGER)
      OR (CAST(substr(lt."term_end",1,4) AS INTEGER) =
          CAST(substr(lt."term_start",1,4) AS INTEGER)
          AND substr(lt."term_end",6,5) >= '12-31')
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. For each qualifying woman, extract her earliest ("first") term and its state.
WITH qualified AS (
    SELECT lt.*
    FROM "legislators_terms" lt
    JOIN "legislators" l
      ON l."id_bioguide" = lt."id_bioguide"
    WHERE l."gender" = 'F'
      AND (
            CAST(substr(lt."term_end",1,4) AS INTEGER) >
            CAST(substr(lt."term_start",1,4) AS INTEGER)
          OR (CAST(substr(lt."term_end",1,4) AS INTEGER) =
              CAST(substr(lt."term_start",1,4) AS INTEGER)
              AND substr(lt."term_end",6,5) >= '12-31')
          )
), first_terms AS (
    SELECT "id_bioguide",
           MIN("term_start") AS first_start
    FROM qualified
    GROUP BY "id_bioguide"
)
SELECT f."id_bioguide",
       q."state",
       f.first_start
FROM first_terms AS f
JOIN qualified   AS q
  ON q."id_bioguide" = f."id_bioguide"
 AND q."term_start"  = f.first_start
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Count how many of those women have each first‑represented state.
WITH qualified AS (
    SELECT lt.*
    FROM "legislators_terms" lt
    JOIN "legislators" l
      ON l."id_bioguide" = lt."id_bioguide"
    WHERE l."gender" = 'F'
      AND (
            CAST(substr(lt."term_end",1,4) AS INTEGER) >
            CAST(substr(lt."term_start",1,4) AS INTEGER)
          OR (CAST(substr(lt."term_end",1,4) AS INTEGER) =
              CAST(substr(lt."term_start",1,4) AS INTEGER)
              AND substr(lt."term_end",6,5) >= '12-31')
          )
), first_terms AS (
    SELECT "id_bioguide",
           MIN("term_start") AS first_start
    FROM qualified
    GROUP BY "id_bioguide"
), first_state AS (
    SELECT ft."id_bioguide",
           q."state"
    FROM first_terms ft
    JOIN qualified q
      ON q."id_bioguide" = ft."id_bioguide"
     AND q."term_start"  = ft.first_start
